    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d784">

                <pb facs="0767" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg601"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.5914/48</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Egan to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-23T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1916, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>220. Referring to my cable of February 17, 1 p.m. Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    pressing urgently for answer to West Indies proposition. He fears that our
                    tension with Germany may delay matters. France ceded all rights to Saint Croix
                    in 1868.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Egan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
